ragh-ú [√ raṅgh = raṃh], a. (v-ī́) speeding, 🞄fleet (V.);
 m. courser (V.);
 N. of an 🞄ancient king, ancestor of Rāma: pl. descendants 🞄of Raghu;
 -tilaka, m. ep. of Rāma;
 🞄-drú, a. running swiftly (RV.): -nandana, 🞄m. descendant of Raghu, ep. of Rāma;
 -nātha, m. ep. of Rāma;
 -pati, m. lord of the 🞄Raghus, ep. of Rāma;
 -pátvan, a. flying 🞄swiftly (RV.);
 -vaṃśa, m. Raghuʼs race T. 🞄of a well-known poem by Kālidāsa: -saṃjīvanī, f. T. of Mallināthaʼs commentary on 🞄the Raghuvaṃśa, -ṣyád, a. gliding swiftly 🞄(V.);
 -svāmin, -uttama, -udvaha, m. ep. 🞄of Rāma.
